    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0587" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5123/2318: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-03-27T16:00:00-05:00">March 27, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. Your telegram 76, February 21, noon [<hi rendition="#italic">4 p.m.</hi>].
                    Treasury Department states that under the Revenue Acts of 1932 and 1934 and <pb
                        facs="0588" n="486" xml:id="pg486"/> Regulations promulgated thereunder
                    British subjects who are nonresident aliens as to the United States and who come
                    here for business purposes are liable for Federal income tax on their income
                    received as compensation for services performed in this country. It is added
                    that while the conclusions set forth appear to be inescapable under existing law
                    consideration is being given to the advisability of recommending to Congress a
                    change which would alleviate the hardships involved.</p>
                <p>A copy of Treasury letter<anchor n="7" xml:id="d369-f1"/> is being forwarded by
                    mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
